<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simla Hill States</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shimla Hill States</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimla">Simla</a> Hill States were a group of small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> in the western Himalayan foothills around Shimla, most of them ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> families. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-nepalese-war">Anglo-Nepalese War</a> of 1814–1816 they came under British protection, supervised by a superintendent at Shimla. In 1948 they were merged to form <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simla-hill-states.jpg" alt="Simla Hill States" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hogweard India Himachal Pradesh relief map.svg: C1MM Rajput Kingdoms of Himachal Pradesh.png: GujaratiHistoryinDNA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajput_states_in_Himachal_Pradesh.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
